The {{Term/Store|Lizalfos Mask||Series, BotW, TotK, AoC}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Allies"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Lizalfos Mask is a piece of [[Armor]] that can be purchased from [[Kilton]] at the [[Fang and Bone]] for 299 [[Mon]] after freeing two [[Divine Beast]]s. It cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]], nor can it be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]]. When worn, it grants [[Link]] the [[Disguise (Mechanic)|Disguise]] [[Added Effect]], allowing him to blend in with [[Lizalfos]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> However, the Lizalfos Mask does not prevent other [[Enemy|Enemies]] in the same area from attacking Link. It also makes quiet Lizalfos sounds as Link moves around. While wearing the Lizalfos Mask, Link adopts a new idle pose to match that of a Lizalfos.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Descriptions TotK}}
The Lizalfos Mask returns in {{TotK|-}}, functioning the same as it did in {{BotW|-}}. It can be obtained from [[Koltin's Stall]] for three [[Bubbul Gem]]s after trading a total of 11 Bubbul Gems for the prior rewards. Subsequent Lizalfos Masks can be purchased from [[Cece]] for 4000 [[Rupee]]s.

==Other Appearances==
==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Descriptions AoC}}
The Lizalfos Mask is a piece of [[Attire]] that can only be worn by [[Link]], and is obtained by completing the [[Quest#Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity|Quest]] "[[Visiting a Special Shop]]". The mask was made by the owner of the [[Fang and Bone]] store.<ref name="AoC Allies"/>
{{Noncanon|End}}

